---
// /admin → Analytics / Comments before the comments API is running: the one-time Cloudflare setup, step by step.
// "Connect now" re-runs the site's deploy workflow, which deploys the API once the secret is there (api/deploy.mjs).
import { API_STATE } from '../config';
const repo = process.env.GITHUB_REPOSITORY || 'obsec07/obsec07.github.io';
const actions = `https://github.com/${repo}/actions/workflows/pages.yml`;
---
<div class="st-card st-guide">
  {API_STATE === 'error' && (
    <div class="acct-note err">The last deploy couldn't set up the comments server. <a href={actions} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the deploy log</a>: the "Comments &amp; stats API" step says why. Usually the token is missing a permission (step 2).</div>
  )}
  <h3>Turn on comments, likes and visitor stats</h3>
  <p>Guests' replies and likes, and visitor stats (IP address, location, pages, devices), need a small server: GitHub Pages can only serve files. It runs free on Cloudflare. One-time setup, about 5 minutes, works from a phone:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Create a free account at <a href="https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dash.cloudflare.com</a> (no card needed) and verify your email.</li>
    <li>In Cloudflare open <a href="https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My Profile → API Tokens</a> → <b>Create Token</b> → <b>Edit Cloudflare Workers</b> → Use template. Under Permissions press <b>+ Add more</b> and pick <b>Account · D1 · Edit</b>. Then <b>Continue to summary</b> → <b>Create Token</b>, and copy the token.</li>
    <li>On GitHub open <a href={`https://github.com/${repo}/settings/secrets/actions/new`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Settings → Secrets → Actions → New repository secret</a>. Name: <code>CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN</code>. Secret: the token. Press <b>Add secret</b>.</li>
    <li>Come back here and press <button type="button" class="save-btn st-connect">Connect now</button> It redeploys the site (by saving a tiny file, <code>api/.redeploy</code>, like saving a post does), which sets up the server. About 2 minutes later reload this page.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="st-connect-msg" role="status"></p>
  {API_STATE === 'off' && (
    <p class="st-note"><b>Pressed Connect now and still see these steps?</b> The last deploy didn't find the secret. It has to be under <b>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Repository secrets</b>, named exactly <code>CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN</code> (not a Variable, and not an Environment secret). Add it there, then press Connect now again.</p>
  )}
  <p class="st-note">The server stores visits for 90 days. Visitors are told about it in the cookie notice and on the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/privacy`}>Privacy</a> page.</p>
</div>
